[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (-2,0) rectangle (3,4);
\draw (-2,0) rectangle (3,4);
\draw[->] (-3.8,0) -- (4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.2) -- (0,5.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-3.6,4) -- (4.6,4);
\node[above] at (4,4.05) {$y=4$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \draw (\x,0.12) -- (\x,-0.12) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4} \draw (0.12,\y) -- (-0.12,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use an area formula to evaluate $\int_{-2}^{3}4\,dx$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, y=0.5cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- (1,4) -- (5,8) -- (5,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.6,0) -- (7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.8) -- (0,11) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-0.5,2.5) -- (6,9);
\node at (2,9) {$y=x+3$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} \draw (\x,0.3) -- (\x,-0.3) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8} \draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use an area formula to evaluate $\int_{1}^{5}(x+3)\,dx$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) arc (0:180:2) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.6,0) -- (3.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.2) -- (0,3.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (2,0) arc (0:180:2);
\node at (2,2.6) {$y=\sqrt{4-x^{2}}$};
\foreach \x in {-2,-1,1,2,3} \draw (\x,0.12) -- (\x,-0.12) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {1,2} \draw (0.12,\y) -- (-0.12,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph of $y=\sqrt{4-x^{2}}$ is the upper half of a circle centred at the origin. Evaluate $\int_{-2}^{2}\sqrt{4-x^{2}}\,dx$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (-1,0) -- (-1,-4) -- (1,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- (2,2) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-2.8,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-5.8) -- (0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-1.4,-4.8) -- (3,4);
\node at (2.6,3.6) {$y=2x-2$};
\foreach \x in {-2,-1,1,2,3} \draw (\x,0.12) -- (\x,-0.12) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {-4,-2,2,4} \draw (0.12,\y) -- (-0.12,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The line $y=2x-2$ crosses the $x$-axis at $x=1$. Find the **value of the definite integral** $\int_{-1}^{2}(2x-2)\,dx$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, y=0.4cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,-6) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) -- (4,6) -- (4,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.6,0) -- (5.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-8.6) -- (0,9.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-0.4,-7.2) -- (4.6,7.8);
\node at (1.2,6) {$y=3x-6$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} \draw (\x,0.3) -- (\x,-0.3) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {-6,-3,3,6} \draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the **total area enclosed** between $y=3x-6$, the $x$-axis, $x=0$ and $x=4$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, y=0.4cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (5,10) -- (5,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.8,0) -- (6.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.6) -- (0,13.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-0.6,-1.2) -- (5.8,11.6);
\node at (1.6,9) {$y=2x$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} \draw (\x,0.3) -- (\x,-0.3) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8,10} \draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The shaded region lies between $y=2x$ and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=5$. Use it to evaluate $\int_{5}^{0}2x\,dx$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,2) -- (2,6) -- (5,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.4,0) -- (6.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.4) -- (0,7.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (0,2) -- (2,6) -- (5,0);
\node at (3.8,5) {$y=f(x)$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} \draw (\x,0.12) -- (\x,-0.12) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {2,4,6} \draw (0.12,\y) -- (-0.12,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph of $y=f(x)$ runs in straight lines from $(0,2)$ to $(2,6)$ and then to $(5,0)$. Evaluate $\int_{0}^{5}f(x)\,dx$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.7cm, y=0.7cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (6,0) arc (0:90:6) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.6,0) -- (8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.6) -- (0,8.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (6,0) arc (0:90:6);
\node at (3.4,7.2) {$y=\sqrt{36-x^{2}}$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6} \draw (\x,0.16) -- (\x,-0.16) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {2,4,6} \draw (0.16,\y) -- (-0.16,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph of $y=\sqrt{36-x^{2}}$ is part of a circle centred at the origin. Evaluate $\int_{0}^{6}\sqrt{36-x^{2}}\,dx$.
